{"type":"text","timestamp":1794352567944,"sessionID":"ses_e384ec77fffej89Mu67UFrzJFG","part":{"id":"prt_1c7bf56790011PYpjz2XPmVddP","messageID":"msg_1c7bf40be001RRzkCi6SQN1Du5","sessionID":"ses_e384ec77fffej89Mu67UFrzJFG","type":"text","text":"There is a potential `UnboundLocalError`: if `optional_text` raises (e.g. `description` is a non-string) then neither `description` nor `location` is assigned, but the code reaches `errors` check and raises `ApiError` first. Actually since `errors` is non-empty, it raises before reaching the return — so no unbound access. But it's fragile and also loses validation of `location` when `description` fails. Let me make it cleaner and collect both errors independently.","time":{"start":1794352567930,"end":1794352567941}}}
